  "answer": "The elongation is calculated as the absolute difference between the Moon and Sun longitudes: |14 - 350| = 336 degrees. Normalized to [0, 360), it remains 336 degrees. Using the tithi formula: Tithi = floor(norm360(Moon longitude - Sun longitude)/12) + 1. Moon - Sun = 14 - 350 = -336. norm360(-336) = 24. Then, floor(24 / 12) + 1 = floor(2) + 1 = 3. Thus, the one-based tithi is 3. The limit of this result is defined by the half-open interval: exactly 24 degrees belongs to tithi 3, meaning the tithi boundary is inclusive at 24 degrees. This result is valid within the specified tithi partitioning rule [EVAL-D05-S1].",
